Truncation toward zero: int(a / b) works but float issues for large ints. Better:
q = abs(a) // abs(b) with sign. Or use math.trunc / int(a/b) — float precision issues for very large numbers. I'll use the integer approach:

if tok == '/':
    q = abs(a) // abs(b)
    if (a < 0) != (b < 0):
        q = -q
    stack.append(q)

That truncates toward zero correctly.

